 # GPU Voxelization with Atomic Accumulation
 
-Also called: Atomic Average for Voxelization, Atomic RGBA8 average voxelization, Atomic Running Average Voxelization, Hardware-accelerated voxelization, Voxelization with Atomic Running Average
+Also called: Atomic RGBA8 Averaging, Atomic Average for Voxelization, Atomic RGBA8 average voxelization, Atomic Voxelization with Averaging, Atomic Running Average Voxelization, Voxelization with Atomic Running Average, Voxelization via Fragment Shader with Image Atomic Operations
 
 ## Overview
-A fragment-shader-based voxelization technique that accumulates per-fragment lighting and material properties into a 3D texture using hardware atomic operations to resolve race conditions and compute a moving average of samples per voxel [S1, S2, unofficial]. It solves the flickering artifact caused by multiple primitives overwriting the same voxel, which occurs because the render order of primitives changes every frame [S2, unofficial]. Unlike simple `imageStore` approaches that discard previous values, this method maintains a consistent lighting approximation for voxels hit by multiple surfaces [S2, unofficial].
+A fragment-shader-based voxelization technique that accumulates per-fragment lighting and material properties into a 3D texture using hardware atomic operations to resolve race conditions and compute a moving average of samples per voxel [S1, S2, unofficial]. It differs from its parent, [GPU Voxelization Using OpenGL Image Atomics](2544-gpu-voxelization-using-opengl-image-atomics.md), by explicitly implementing a moving average via `imageAtomicCompSwap` loops to prevent flickering when multiple primitives overwrite the same voxel, rather than relying solely on conservative rasterization or simple max operations [S1, S4, unofficial].
 
 ## How it works
 **Inputs:**
-*   3D polygonal mesh geometry (vertices, normals, texture coordinates) [G].
-*   Material properties (`ambient`, `diffuse`, `specular`, `transmittance`, `emission`, `shininess`, `ior`, `dissolve`, `illum`, `roughness`, `metallic`, `sheen`, `clearcoat_thickness`, `clearcoat_roughness`, `anisotropy`, `anisotropy_rotation`) [S1, unofficial].
-*   Light sources (`position`, `color`, `intensity`) [S1, unofficial].
-*   Scene bounds and voxel grid dimensions (`dim`) [S1, unofficial].
-*   `cube_size`: Uniform float scaling factor for light positions [S1, unofficial].
-*   `illum`: Integer material illumination mode [S1, unofficial].
+- 3D triangle mesh geometry.
+- Material properties (diffuse color, emission, transparency mode).
+- Light sources (position, color, intensity).
+- Scene parameters (voxel resolution, view matrices, shadow maps).
 
 **Outputs:**
-*   Six 3D textures (`tex3D[6]`), bound as `uimage3D` with `r32ui` format [S1, unofficial].
+- A 3D texture (or array of 3D textures) storing voxel data in `RGBA8` format (packed into `uint`).
+- A sparse list of occupied voxel coordinates.
 
 **Data Structures:**
-*   **Material Uniform Block (`std140`, binding=1):**
